I've made the following changes to the TopicStatusRepositoryImpl.java file:

  1. Changed the first instance of returning a merged entity from:
  status.setViewed(viewed);
  session.merge(status);
  return status;
  1. to:
  status.setViewed(viewed);
  return session.merge(status);
  2. Changed the second instance of returning a merged entity (in the catch block) from:
  status.setViewed(viewed);
  session.merge(status);
  return status;
  2. to:
  status.setViewed(viewed);
  return session.merge(status);
  3. Changed the Hibernate-specific save method to the JPA standard persist method:
  session.save(newStatus);
  3. to:
  session.persist(newStatus);

  These changes follow best practices by:
  1. Always returning the managed entity from merge() operations
  2. Using JPA standard methods (persist) instead of Hibernate-specific ones (save)

