**Date parsing: avoid always appending 'Z' (can corrupt valid ISO strings)**

Instant.parse already handles ISO-8601 with offsets/Z. Appending "Z" unconditionally makes strings like "2025-05-10T04:59:59Z" invalid ("...ZZ"). Parse robustly and default to UTC when no offset is present.

```diff
