-            Instant dueDate = now.plus(30, ChronoUnit.DAYS); // default to 1 month from now
-            if (dueDateStr != null && !dueDateStr.trim().isEmpty()) {
-                try {
-                    // Canvas uses ISO 8601 format: 2025-05-10T04:59:59
-                    dueDate = Instant.parse(dueDateStr.trim() + "Z"); // Add Z for UTC if not present
-                } catch (Exception e) {
-                    log.warn("Failed to parse Canvas due date: {}, using default", dueDateStr);
-                }
-            }
+            String dueDateStr = assignmentXml.getChildText("due_at", canvasNs);
+            Instant dueDate = now.plus(30, ChronoUnit.DAYS); // default to 1 month from now
+            if (dueDateStr != null && !dueDateStr.trim().isEmpty()) {
+                Instant parsed = parseCanvasInstant(dueDateStr.trim());
+                if (parsed != null) {
+                    dueDate = parsed;
+                } else {
+                    log.warn("Failed to parse Canvas due date: {}, using default", dueDateStr);
+                }
+            }
```

Add this helper (outside this hunk) to centralize parsing:

```java
// Helper to parse Canvas ISO timestamps with or without offset; defaults to UTC when none supplied
private static Instant parseCanvasInstant(String ts) {
    try {
        // If it already has 'Z' or an offset like +hh:mm or -hh:mm, Instant.parse will work
        if (ts.endsWith("Z") || ts.matches(".*[+-]\\d\\d:\\d\\d$")) {
            return Instant.parse(ts);
        }
        // Parse local date-time and assume UTC
        return java.time.LocalDateTime.parse(ts).atOffset(java.time.ZoneOffset.UTC).toInstant();
    } catch (Exception ignored) {
        return null;
    }
}
```

