🌐 Web query:

`In Apache Commons IO 2.22.0, does the deprecated constructor BOMInputStream(InputStream) declare `throws IOException`, or is IOException only thrown by BOMInputStream.Builder.get()?`

💡 Result:

In Apache Commons IO 2.22.0, the deprecated constructor BOMInputStream(InputStream) does not declare throws IOException. It takes a single InputStream parameter with no checked exceptions in its signature, consistent with earlier versions like 2.21.0 and the current master branch source code. The IOException is only thrown by BOMInputStream.Builder.get, which builds and potentially opens the underlying InputStream, throwing IOException if an I/O error occurs during conversion or opening (e.g., from Path or File).

Citations:

- 1: https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-io/apidocs/org/apache/commons/io/input/BOMInputStream.html
- 2: http://commons.apache.org/io/apidocs/org/apache/commons/io/input/BOMInputStream.Builder.html
