_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_ | _🏗️ Heavy lift_

**Regression: any non-in-progress LTI score callback now marks the assignment as student-submitted.**

`handleAssignment` is reached for every LTI score update, including instructor-initiated grade pushes via `setGrade` / `handleGradebookLTI13`, not only student submission events. With the new branch:

- When `activityProgress` is anything other than `INITIALIZED/STARTED/INPROGRESS`, the code unconditionally calls `submission.setSubmitted(true)`.
- The default for `activityProgress` is `ACTIVITY_COMPLETED` (line 2840), so a tool that simply pushes a grade without sending an explicit `activityProgress` will land here.
- If `previousDateSubmitted == null` (student never submitted), `dateSubmitted` is then set to `now`, fabricating a student submission timestamp from an instructor/tool grading event.

This matches the regression flagged in the PR review (and motivated the alternative PR `#14573`). The transition needs to factor in (a) whether `activityProgress` was explicitly provided vs. defaulted, and (b) the actor/role context, before flipping `submitted` from false→true. Preserving an existing `dateSubmitted` (the stated intent of SAK-52505) can be done without forcing `submitted=true` on every non-in-progress callback — e.g. only adjust `submitted`/`dateSubmitted` when `activityProgress` was explicitly `SUBMITTED`/`COMPLETED`, and otherwise leave the prior submission state alone.

