🌐 Web query:

`In Spring MVC with Jackson, if a JSON request body omits a primitive boolean field, what value is bound by default, and how is this different from java.lang.Boolean?`

💡 Result:

In Spring MVC with Jackson, the behavior when a JSON request body omits a boolean field depends on whether the field is a primitive boolean or a wrapper Boolean [1]. Primitive boolean: When a primitive boolean field is omitted from the JSON request body, Jackson binds it to its Java default value, which is false [2][1]. Because it is a primitive, it cannot be null [1]. java.lang.Boolean: When a wrapper Boolean field is omitted from the JSON request body, Jackson binds it to null [1]. Unlike the primitive type, the wrapper class allows for a null state, which is often used to distinguish between a field that was explicitly set to false and one that was not provided at all [1]. Key Differences: 1. Default Value: Primitive boolean defaults to false, while java.lang.Boolean defaults to null [1]. 2. Nullability: Primitive boolean is non-nullable, whereas java.lang.Boolean is nullable [1]. 3. Configuration: You can change the behavior for primitives by enabling the DeserializationFeature.FAIL_ON_NULL_FOR_PRIMITIVES feature [3][4]. When this is enabled, Jackson will throw an exception if it encounters a null value for a primitive field, though this feature's interaction with completely absent fields can sometimes be nuanced depending on the Jackson version [5][4]. Best Practice: If you need to distinguish between a missing field and an explicit false value, use the wrapper java.lang.Boolean [1]. If the field is mandatory and should always be present, you can use `[user]`(required = true) to force Jackson to throw an exception if the field is missing [3].

Citations:

- 1: https://dev.to/abhishek_shahi_9d131e426d/boolean-field-becomes-null-in-spring-boot-dto-heres-why-and-how-to-fix-it-4i39
- 2: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/33156893/spring-boolean-variables-in-objects-get-returned
- 3: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/75659006/jackson-defaulting-empty-or-null-value-of-boolean-field-to-false
- 4: https://github.com/[user]/spring-cloud-aws/issues/1553
- 5: https://github.com/[user]/jackson-databind/issues/5734

