**Preserve input wall-clock parts before Sakai timezone resolution.**

`DateHelper.normalize` converts ISO input to a browser-local `Date`. A browser DST gap can change the entered time before `formatForSakai` resolves the Sakai timezone. For example, `2027-03-14T02:30` becomes `03:30` in `America/New_York`, then serializes as `03:30` for `Europe/Berlin`. Retain the input components independently and add this cross-timezone DST-gap test.

