**Reject invalid localized calendar dates.**

`parseDate` tries both localized formatters before the ISO fallback. Both formatter factories use `ResolverStyle.SMART` by default. For a month/day/year locale such as `Locale.US`, `2/30/26` can resolve to February 28. The import path then applies that value to the poll opening or closing time instead of raising `INVALID_DATES`. The ISO fallback does not prevent this because it runs only after localized parsing fails.

Use strict resolution for both localized formats. When deriving strict patterns, convert year-of-era `y` tokens to proleptic-year `u` tokens while preserving their widths, such as `yy` to `uu` and `yyyy` to `uuuu`. Strict parsing cannot resolve a `y` pattern without an era.

