✅ Addressed in commit ae67f77

_📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Make the `finally` cleanup safe to run when setup fails.**

`assignmentService.deleteAssignment(assignment)` runs outside a transaction, because this test uses `Propagation.NOT_SUPPORTED`. The call also needs the `SECURE_REMOVE_ASSIGNMENT` stub, which `createPublishedGroupAssignment` sets. The main problem is that `finally` runs this cleanup even after an earlier assertion fails. If cleanup then throws, for example a `PermissionException` or a Hibernate session error, that exception replaces the original assertion failure. The test report then hides the real cause. Wrap the cleanup in its own `transaction.execute` call, and catch and log any cleanup exception so the original failure is still reported.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-            assignmentService.deleteAssignment(assignment);
+            try {
+                transaction.executeWithoutResult(status -> {
+                    try {
+                        assignmentService.deleteAssignment(assignment);
+                    } catch (PermissionException e) {
+                        throw new IllegalStateException(e);
+                    }
+                });
+            } catch (RuntimeException e) {
+                log.warn("Cleanup failed for assignment {}", assignment.getId(), e);
+            }
```
</details>

